A||||4||burdell1||Car Won't Start....Please help!
Z||000000||burdell1||07-22-99||11:05 AM||||In the past few weeks, my '85 Fiero GT would seem to jerk slightly when at certain speeds. It was so subtle, however, that most of the time I wasn't sure if it wasn't in my mind. Then yesterday it got worse and would hesitate when I was idling for long periods of time at stop lights and the Check Engine light would flash on and off.  When I got home, I checked with a code reader and all I got was 12.  So then I started up the car again, and when I shut it off, there was a popping sound. I tried to start it again, and then it wouldn't start at all. It seems like the car isn't getting any fuel. I've had the fuel pump replaced twice in the last year, so I was hoping it was that (because it is still under warranty.) However, if it is that, what would cause it to go out so often.
Z||000001||burdell1||07-22-99||01:10 PM||||I forgot to mention that it turns over at a good rate of speed (so it is probably not the battery). Also, I even tried pressing down the gas pedal a few times, but there was no smell of gas at all. That is what makes me think (and hope) it is the fuel pump/<br>
Z||000002||DJRice||07-22-99||03:01 PM||||Could be fuel, but I would check the timing too.  Popping could be backfires?  Check your rotor under the distributor cap, I actually had one break and I thought that the car was dying violently but it was an easy fix.  <p>Also there was a post about multiple dying fuel pumps a while back.....look that up.
Z||000003||burdell1||07-22-99||04:16 PM||||I can't find that string on the dying fuel pumps. What is the name of that post?<br>
Z||000004||DJRice||07-23-99||10:12 AM||||My bad, It wasnt fuel pumps....sorry, it was starters......  Oops.  
